-- Demo data: two stores in different countries, each with five totems and its
-- own products.
--
-- There is no shared catalog. Each store owns its rows outright: its own
-- product ids, names, prices and stock. Nothing here can change what the other
-- store sells.
--
-- LOCAL-0001 keeps the original ids, USD prices and deliberately uneven stock
-- (one item down to a single unit, one sold out), so the last-unit race and the
-- sold-out path are reachable from a fresh seed.
--
-- BR-SP-0001 proves the point: Portuguese product names, BRL prices, its own
-- stock, and one product fewer.

TRUNCATE order_items, payments, orders, stock, products, totems, stores
  RESTART IDENTITY CASCADE;

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Stores and their totems
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

   'US', 'us-local', 'UTC', 'USD', 'en-US', 0),
  ('a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002', 'BR-SP-0001', 'Snack Bar Paulista',
   'BR', 'br-south-east', 'America/Sao_Paulo', 'BRL', 'pt-BR', 0);


